  "decision": "Prefill clears the floor at 1.41x. Decode does NOT: 15.98 against 58.30 tok/s, so mx is 3.65x faster. The fused Q5_K dot is a real 51% improvement over the previous llmx build and still leaves Q5_K decode far below the external gate. ROADMAP #8's performance requirement is NOT met for Q5_K decode.",
  "hypothesis": "UNVERIFIED. mx quantizes the activation vector to 8-bit and takes an integer dot product, so its inner loop is integer SIMD over two quantized operands. The llmx fused dot converts weights to float and uses float FMA against f32 activations, which moves more bytes per weight and does less work per instruction. This needs measurement before it is treated as the cause.",
